name 'building-data-driven-systems-preassessment-q14_2025'

question 'What is the result of "chaining" a `.filter()` and a `.map()` method together?'

right 'The data is first narrowed down, and then only that smaller subset is transformed into HTML'
wrong 'The original array is deleted, and two new arrays are created in its place.'
wrong 'The code will fail because JavaScript can only handle one array method at a time.'
wrong 'The `.map()` method will run first, followed by the `.filter()` method.'

allow_multiple_attempts false

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 10

Chaining allows data to flow through a "pipeline." The first method (filter) passes its result to the second method (map), allowing for complex operations in a single line of code.
MARKDOWN
